---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Orchestral HR Consulting"
  description="What Orchestral HR Consulting collects when you use this site, why, where it goes, and how to ask us to change or delete it."
  current="privacy"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1>How we handle your information.</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        Short version: we collect what you send us, we use it to reply, and nothing on this
        site tracks you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--flush">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="legal reveal">
        <p class="legal-date">Last updated 3 October 2026</p>

        <h2>What this covers</h2>
        <p>
          This policy applies to <strong>orchestralhr.ca</strong> &mdash; what happens when you
          visit the site or get in touch through it.
        </p>
        <p>
          It does <strong>not</strong> cover personal information we handle on behalf of a client
          organisation under a services agreement, such as employee records or candidate
          information. That is governed by the agreement with the client concerned and the data
          handling terms within it.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <dl class="legal-dl">
          <dt>When you use the contact form</dt>
          <dd>
            Your name, company, job title and email address, plus an optional description of what
            you would like help with. All of it is information you choose to give us.
          </dd>

          <dt>When you email us directly</dt>
          <dd>Whatever you choose to include in your message.</dd>

          <dt>Automatically</dt>
          <dd>
            This site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which records standard server information such as
            IP address and browser type in the course of serving pages. We have no access to those
            logs and do not use them.
          </dd>
        </dl>

        <p class="legal-note">
          We do not use analytics. We do not set cookies. We do not load fonts, scripts or
          embeds from third-party networks &mdash; everything this site needs is served from the
          site itself. There is no tracking here, and nothing follows you after you leave.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>
          Solely to respond to your enquiry and, if it leads somewhere, to continue that
          conversation. We do not sell it, rent it, trade it, or add it to a marketing list.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it goes</h2>
        <p>
          The contact form is processed by <strong>Formspree</strong>, a third-party service that
          receives your submission and forwards it to us by email. This means the information you
          enter is transmitted to and stored on servers in the <strong>United States</strong>,
          where it may be accessible to US courts and authorities under the laws of that country.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you would rather your enquiry did not pass through a service outside Canada, email
          <a href="mailto:info@orchestralhr.ca">info@orchestralhr.ca</a> directly instead.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our email is hosted on Google Workspace. We do not share your information with anyone
          else unless you ask us to, or unless we are required to by law.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Enquiries that do not lead to an engagement are deleted within 24 months. Where a
          conversation becomes a client relationship, records are retained under the terms of the
          agreement with that client.
        </p>

        <h2>How we protect it</h2>
        <p>
          Access is limited to the people who need it. Accounts require multi-factor
          authentication, and our email is authenticated with SPF, DKIM and DMARC so that
          messages claiming to come from us can be verified as genuine.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask what personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us
          to delete it. Write to
          <a href="mailto:privacy@orchestralhr.ca">privacy@orchestralhr.ca</a> and we will respond
          within 30 days, as the <em>Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents
          Act</em> requires.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are not satisfied with our response, you may complain to the Office of the
          Privacy Commissioner of Canada at
          <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca" rel="noopener">priv.gc.ca</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Unsolicited commercial email</h2>
        <p>
          The email addresses published on this site are here so that clients and prospective
          clients can reach us. Publishing them is <strong>not</strong> consent to receive
          commercial electronic messages, and they may not be collected or used for that purpose.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, we will update the date at the top of this page.
        </p>

        <h2>Who is accountable</h2>
        <p class="legal-contact">
          Valerie Khan, Privacy Officer<br />
          <a href="mailto:privacy@orchestralhr.ca">privacy@orchestralhr.ca</a><br />
          Orchestral HR Consulting &middot; Ontario, Canada
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .legal-date {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 38px;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 44px 0 14px;
  }

  .legal h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--crimson-text);
  }

  .legal strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .legal-dl {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }

  .legal-dl dt {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15.5px;
    margin: 20px 0 6px;
  }

  .legal-dl dd {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal-note {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--crimson-dim);
    padding-left: 18px;
    margin: 28px 0 16px;
  }

  .legal-contact {
    line-height: 1.9;
  }
</style>
